WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:16.939
On the eleventh day of Christmas, we have
element number eleven, sodium. Not a

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:24.590
piece of sodium, a tile with sodium on it
and sodium is element number 11 and it

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:28.689
really is a tile, look on the back. It
was made by an Italian school girl

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:35.410
called Sofia who was brought here by
her father Leonardo plus a school friend

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.320
and other family members.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:44.080
She's a real Periodic Videos fan and
she wanted to come for her birthday to

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:52.129
Nottingham and she made this tile for me
so I could put my mug on top of it and

00:00:52.129 --> 00:00:57.460
the reason why she chose sodium is
because she saw in a video, our sodium

00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:01.460
video, that I said that sodium was my
favorite element

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:03.960
- Holy crap

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.620
- Not because it explodes, but because my mother's first name, her Christian

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:10.880
name was Ina, I-N-A,

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.840
and as a little girl she used to call herself Na and my children used to call their

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:23.790
grandmother Na because of this, so every
time I see the symbol Na, N-A, I get

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:30.670
just a warm motherly feeling and Sophia liked this and made me a great tile. So I have

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:37.490
it on my desk and I brought it down here
specially for the eleventh day. So number eleven,

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.729
tile with sodium, two elements

00:01:40.729 --> 00:01:46.109
osmium and thorium, periodic table handkerchief, charred beam from our carbon lab,

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:53.960
fan from a fan, element six carbon, glowing plectrum for guitar, four drinking vessels,

00:01:53.960 --> 00:02:04.960
three chemical badges, two periodic table bed covers, and one piece of tartaric acid from a Swiss wine barrel.

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:09.810
Let's see what we have for day twelve!

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:21.520
...tiny droplets of metallic sodium

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:24.050
and as these droplets go through the air

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:27.720
some of them will react with the water vapor
in the air

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.680
and some will react with the oxygen in the air, and

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.469
there's a lot more oxygen than water...

